A compact bookkeeping version is $\begin{aligned}
\Delta \mathcal{C}_t
&=
\{\text{skill learned}\}
\cup
\{\text{person or mentor}\}
\cup
\{\text{help given}\},\\
\mathcal{C}_{t+1}
&=
\mathcal{C}_t\cup\Delta \mathcal{C}_t.\end{aligned}$ Here $\mathcal{C}_t$ is not a dollar value. It is a source-conscious notation for portable career capital: what a person can carry forward after the present job or company changes.

