The sequence in lecture 108 is: $\text{growth scan}
\longrightarrow
\text{study}
\longrightarrow
\text{foot in the door}
\longrightarrow
\text{fit test}
\longrightarrow
\text{build or stay involved}.$ That last phrase matters. Mitt says it did not have to be starting a business; it only had to be involvement in those industries. This keeps the arena-selection chapter from becoming founder-first too quickly. The first rational move may be proximity, not incorporation.

