A cautious reconstruction of the comparison is: $\begin{aligned}
C_{T|F} &\approx D_J,\\
C_N &\approx D_J + R_N,\end{aligned}$ where $C_{T|F}$ is the cost of trying and then failing, $C_N$ is the cost of not trying, and $D_J$ is the burden of returning to a job. Subtracting gives $\begin{aligned}
C_N-C_{T|F}
&\approx (D_J+R_N)-D_J\\
&=R_N.\end{aligned}$ So if the regret term is real, $R_N>0
\qquad\Longrightarrow\qquad
C_N>C_{T|F}$ inside this limited decision frame.

