The next move is the cleanest runway mechanism in the series so far. He sells the one asset he names, a motorcycle, and says that got them through another month or two. Let $A_{\mathrm{moto}}$ denote the proceeds from that sale and $B$ the monthly burn rate. The cash update is $C_1=C_0+A_{\mathrm{moto}}.$ The added runway is reconstructed as $\Delta R_{\mathrm{moto}}
\approx
\frac{A_{\mathrm{moto}}}{B}
\approx
1\text{ to }2\ \hbox{months}.$ This is not a motorcycle valuation. The transcript supplies the duration, not the sale price or burn rate. The useful mechanism is narrower and stronger: a non-cash asset becomes operating time.

